ing to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{36}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}[v]_{u^{2}}^{36}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}(36)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}(36 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 36 u]_{-6}^{6} \\\\ &=1(((216)+(-72))-((-216)+(72))) \\\\ &=1(288) \\\\ &=288\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674197} {:answer/id #uuid "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674201} {:answer/id #uuid "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674211} {:answer/id #uuid "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674218} {:answer/id #uuid "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{500}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674220}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674211} :answer-field/id #uuid "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the curve $(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0$ and the line $y=4.$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nSubstituting $x - 8 y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0\\,⟹\\,u^{2}-v=0\\,⟹\\,v=u^{2}.\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\nv=4.\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}v=u^{2} \\\\ v=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 2,4).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/b4/b43c84eb76241233dc88e2d6a94bc4e5e24d558f8c9f46a826d0d928059aefc2.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}1&-8\\\\0&1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{4}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}[v]_{u^{2}}^{4}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}(4)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}(4 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 4 u]_{-2}^{2} \\\\ &=1(((8)+(- \\frac{8}{3}))-((-8)+(\\frac{8}{3}))) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8e8400-219c-5335-b307-e56c8ab8b831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684305} {:answer/id #uuid "892370d3-42f1-5e13-b0ee-733b955a5f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684307} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b7eeec-9082-518f-91db-5745e5e627ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684308} {:answer/id #uuid "c17d17a6-28ba-580e-a51f-3d1bfb6e34e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684311} {:answer/id #uuid "eb90f1cb-d820-5339-bcbf-57c8bdd90ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684314}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684314} :answer-field/id #uuid "53101748-589e-523e-a52c-68712b793641" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "21413f34-89d4-5361-9cbf-90133e162d51" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac17a5c3ebae52349c2572235271ce3ae66d10a82e703676b42dab77ff5ced64.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "Every arrow points down and left, and the arrows have the same length and direction throughout the diagram.\n\n- The horizontal component is negative. This rules out $H$, whose horizontal component is positive, and $K$, whose horizontal component is zero.\n- The vertical component is negative. This rules out $F$, whose vertical component is positive.\n\nBoth components are constant, so the matching function is\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=-\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "841d4560-b6c8-5a29-a66c-affa13d6f9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684306} {:answer/id #uuid "bf87a67e-1c32-597b-8ced-8279602bd866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684310} {:answer/id #uuid "ec974037-d29f-5b17-a88a-12df7542e18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684315} {:answer/id #uuid "ee98cc4a-7ea5-52c5-b293-19a7cbf47e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684316} {:answer/id #uuid "f28d320c-91e0-57ee-971b-7bfa9c48d67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684315} :answer-field/id #uuid "63a2ef78-f33f-5af1-ace7-ac6c5b3695da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a1a5396-0188-5490-88df-cbca12d1e87e" :question/problem "![](images/66/66f74a13da54fafcdd3989878c69aaf4e6bdb57cb8fe44725b35fbb560b618dc.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "All arrows are horizontal, so we compare their horizontal components at different locations.\n\n- Above the $x$-axis the arrows point right, while below it they point left. This rules out the constant fields $F$ and $H$: $F$ always points right, and $H$ always points left.\n- For positive $y$, the horizontal component is positive. This rules out $G(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}$, which points left above the $x$-axis.\n\nAs a further check, arrows in each horizontal row are identical, and their lengths increase with distance from the $x$-axis. Thus the horizontal component changes with $y$, with its sign matching the sign of $y$, and is zero on the $x$-axis. The matching function is\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8abbf3-ba05-5225-bd84-8e433a68bf67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684297} {:answer/id #uuid "305e26d2-13aa-5761-b69a-c4712fbe97f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684299} {:answer/id #uuid "585172f0-6a77-56ab-8a3a-87f01657d250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf{i}-y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684303} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d10b5c-45df-5124-8cc9-c0edc6866f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684312} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ec01b4-9d58-550c-8dda-396fb261be43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684313} :answer-field/id #uuid "bba935e4-a7f7-5c9f-9568-59c1049e10e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "57dcad93-a11b-5182-9fee-803a91e37657" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b056c72881c0a31d7bcd29a1f8edd887edf5b415340558969bbe0b1723d51a69.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We need to match both components, since the arrows change direction across the plane.\n\n- On the positive $y$-axis, the arrows point right. This rules out $G$, which points left there, and $H$, which points down there. Both $F$ and $K$ remain possible from this observation alone.\n- On the positive $x$-axis, the arrows point down. This rules out $K$, which points up there. This observation alone would leave $F$ and $G$, but $G$ was already ruled out on the positive $y$-axis. Hence $F$ is the only listed function consistent with both axes.\n\nWe can also check the component patterns away from the axes. The horizontal component is positive above the $x$-axis, negative below it, and grows in magnitude with $|y|$; within each row it stays constant. The vertical component is negative to the right of the $y$-axis, positive to its left, and grows in magnitude with $|x|$; within each column it stays constant. At the origin both components are zero.\n\nThese checks agree with\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f4493d-61f1-5e0b-85b0-7b47e95c7040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684978} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab2d2aa-cba7-5782-8123-919384bf12c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684981} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c86c12-a6ca-5278-9a82-dc64086dd329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684984} {:answer/id #uuid "d829d74e-7ee5-58f9-9cec-dd45d15050bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684986} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0093d7-d8c4-5d4c-a73e-1da36a3c1727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684987}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684978} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb6f14b4-92f4-5724-aa54-560fd8e40770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "00e2635b-8226-5272-92fd-40ef12aca84d" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d26eff05658cee07957b536af454b14c68287d080d2ce7f70f97aec1abd0f913.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) is positive and stays constant across the plane. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y)&=-i-2\\,j \\\\ K(x,y)&=-j \\\\ H(x,y)&=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) is positive and stays constant across the plane.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=i+j.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097979ed-64c4-5da3-b5d0-d25880ce7e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684977} {:answer/id #uuid "1994483f-0385-5c70-ac3c-455b5ee48e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684979} {:answer/id #uuid "82946011-5818-5461-8c07-54b384bc8358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684983} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d9188b-ae8a-5a57-896c-19d7ebea63bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684985} {:answer/id #uuid "eefce3f3-6fdb-5e66-a9d0-7e74be232cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684988}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684977} :answer-field/id #uuid "768df014-c814-50e3-af87-cd0011c6b791" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "55f1737a-6204-5790-b266-c82a398d25fa" :question/problem "![](images/36/36c9003fd50c9b3bb70dbed870876d71fd93130f16335eac34c20869ea8b14e8.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) is negative and stays constant across the plane. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(x,y)&=i+j \\\\ K(x,y)&=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) is negative and stays constant across the plane. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=-i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $F(x,y)=-i-2\\,j.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022fdf22-a01d-52c9-a87c-c4f2ca30e4b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf{i}-y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684991} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff3ebf4-3007-5488-a8a8-5ca867a3d4e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}-y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684995} {:answer/id #uuid "8b16730c-fea7-56db-b504-1d892b13306a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685003} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f84432-c98d-5708-82a5-0dcb26c82c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685013} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e3dce2-b14f-5877-91c8-9eb24095e927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685017} :answer-field/id #uuid "858c7180-aaf9-5617-9362-91dc7f516d58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5b55f288-96fa-55ba-90dc-3d9c16a94d7f" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cf8da09a26e734ce65f67a499a9ebf0f43ae7560dbdda11ce0339ee224f9c528.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) varies with the horizontal coordinate $x$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $x=0$, where it is zero. It is positive when $x>0$ and negative when $x<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y)&=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ K(x,y)&=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}-y\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) varies with the horizontal coordinate $x$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $x=0$, where it is zero. It is positive when $x>0$ and negative when $x<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf{i}-y\\,\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=x\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a54747e3-ebb0-5c95-bc83-a8e70f5e5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685006} {:answer/id #uuid "b958d8c7-9c7a-5942-85a4-febc45fef992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685007} {:answer/id #uuid "d67e0d94-1bdf-5f4d-8f7d-b5ca8d10615c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685010} {:answer/id #uuid "d7cc4dee-07b8-5eb2-b51f-99605d6ef50a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685011} {:answer/id #uuid "f4db1752-25b1-5178-8c1f-0cc9e933577d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685006} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e8885c3-e497-52de-a7a7-89f156b33063" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8151d363-d8ed-5af7-9882-357e249f86b0" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4891b9b900304e5fbd2e70051bb422b9e77b2082374f2ece1ce360fd2010317.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) varies with the vertical coordinate $y$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $y=0$, where it is zero. It is negative when $y>0$ and positive when $y<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H(x,y)&=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ K(x,y)&=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) varies with the vertical coordinate $y$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $y=0$, where it is zero. It is positive when $y>0$ and negative when $y<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40cab428-8ed8-5d02-8de3-93e209f89663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684994} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5ff2c0-8303-5773-8d71-fd5d6e69821b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684997} {:answer/id #uuid "87bbd627-ba39-5c05-b64c-cf0e92b5a452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685002} {:answer/id #uuid "c30981c5-e6c6-5188-b7d4-9412aa1b855e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685009} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ad9c8c-794c-5281-a95e-3be4c5ffc5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685016}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685016} :answer-field/id #uuid "90c4658a-8405-5681-b0ac-e9cd469dcee1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9797f2bd-3767-5d0f-a8a9-5153ccf979e2" :question/problem "![](images/fc/fc2d6f58dc09ecb378d91c26b48107b0c31d72d2b4231d1ccc0357ebbdbc6b24.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) varies with the horizontal coordinate $x$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $x=0$, where it is zero. It is negative when $x>0$ and positive when $x<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y)&=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ G(x,y)&=-y\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) varies with the vertical coordinate $y$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $y=0$, where it is zero. It is positive when $y>0$ and negative when $y<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+x\\,\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d6d8fd-e8da-5551-9537-2675ce9db58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684992} {:answer/id #uuid "238d3ef5-757e-51d2-b3c6-4ba136655e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684993} {:answer/id #uuid "86a1609b-08fd-5a5e-8da3-18acb742acc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685001} {:answer/id #uuid "bf51fece-884f-597e-b9dd-3405cc1b3455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=y\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685008} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a5c60a-8ebe-5d85-aa1a-6da8df19acd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684992} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae6e091-9a45-54cf-8344-bbf6575b4882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f66399c2-a1c5-5165-8fb9-058d62838fd9" :question/problem "![](images/6c/6c156d9f0830e402074b01d4813b69b70adab5f63a27056a6a3ae6f3bd464f14.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nDots denote zero vectors." :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) varies with the horizontal coordinate $x$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $x=0$, where it is zero. It is negative when $x>0$ and positive when $x<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y)&=y\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ G(x,y)&=y\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) varies with the horizontal coordinate $x$. Its magnitude grows as we move away from $x=0$, where it is zero. It is negative when $x>0$ and positive when $x<0$. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf{i}-x\\,\\mathbf{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c0ed9ac-4cd3-5ba1-b481-28b42b467efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=-\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685019} {:answer/id #uuid "2192d963-0cd3-584e-a0e2-6c793c53abb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf G(x,y,z)=-x^2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685020} {:answer/id #uuid "315d261c-7945-5e2b-88db-97608d449f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685022} {:answer/id #uuid "52b57559-84f3-5abf-92ca-5b9cb5bbb5ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf K(x,y,z)=\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685025} {:answer/id #uuid "56de3be7-e17e-53c1-88bc-92220641aef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf H(x,y,z)=\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685022} :answer-field/id #uuid "6828ad01-9669-5287-a1b6-4ac603a64d71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8deedd6a-0545-50c3-a23a-75c82ece094d" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f89653698d9c2bad0c2e6a77d4dad1953a9fd72f89cbfc08fd68aac802acd284.png)\n\nWhich of the following could generate the vector field above? Check each proposed field against the arrows throughout the diagram.\n\nArrow lengths are drawn using a common display scale; no numerical magnitude is specified." :question/worked-solution "The arrows are parallel to the $y$-axis, point opposite its positive direction, and keep the same nonzero length throughout the diagram. A matching field must have zero $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf k$ components and a constant negative $\\mathbf j$ component.\n\n- $\\mathbf F=-\\mathbf k$ points along the $z$-axis, so it has the wrong direction.\n- $\\mathbf G=-x^2\\,\\mathbf j$ has the right axis and points in the negative $y$-direction when $x\\ne0$. However, its length is $x^2$, so it varies as $x$ changes and is zero at $x=0$. The diagram instead shows nonzero arrows of equal length, including on the plane $x=0$.\n- $\\mathbf H=\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j$ has a nonzero $\\mathbf i$ component, so its arrows are not parallel to the $y$-axis.\n- $\\mathbf K=\\mathbf j$ points in the positive $y$-direction, opposite the arrows.\n\nEvery formula is ruled out, so the correct response is **None of the listed**. A constant field such as $-\\mathbf j$ would have the observed pattern, but it is not among the listed formulas."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d3afe2-ca63-5679-a398-0f412e914c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf G(x,y,z)=\\mathbf i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685021} {:answer/id #uuid "4aa68f91-46c8-5272-96f8-d0741a5f7606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685024} {:answer/id #uuid "a9383c81-221f-5c61-a322-6b3b6201629d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=-y\\,\\mathbf i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685034} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc86a68-bd92-57b3-ba10-24a1de153e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf H(x,y,z)=-\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685036} {:answer/id #uuid "df153a23-d264-50cb-a558-fdab14c1769d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf K(x,y,z)=-\\mathbf i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685038} :answer-field/id #uuid "69115854-19b4-5813-a84d-edbb3b3215f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bda2e6f7-7a37-5bb2-a980-19e55d5d673a" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bff60466ca8abba4fd849c046c02af3a4811279774975fc981cafad91d734ed5.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\nArrow lengths are drawn using a common display scale; no numerical magnitude is specified." :question/worked-solution "The arrows are parallel to the $x$-axis, so their $\\mathbf j$ and $\\mathbf k$ components are zero. This rules out $\\mathbf H=-\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j$, which has a nonzero $\\mathbf j$ component.\n\nThe positive $x$-axis points toward the lower left; the arrows point the other way. Their $\\mathbf i$ component is therefore negative, ruling out $\\mathbf G=\\mathbf i$.\n\nThe arrows have the same length and direction throughout the diagram, including across different $y$-positions. The field $\\mathbf F=-y\\,\\mathbf i$ would instead change its magnitude with $y$, vanish at $y=0$, and reverse direction across that plane. It does not fit.\n\nThus $\\mathbf K(x,y,z)=-\\mathbf i$ could generate the diagram: it is constant and points in the negative $x$-direction. “None of the listed” is incorrect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1439e8-c3d6-5d3f-be37-452dbf26cd08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=-\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685023} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9ca757-a61e-5ee2-b044-7cffe775dd3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685030} {:answer/id #uuid "8db22ead-96f1-540a-b1fb-316a7ee0999a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf H(x,y,z)=\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685031} {:answer/id #uuid "9152935b-e035-5192-9b0c-6a6166ca9acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf G(x,y,z)=\\mathbf i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685033} {:answer/id #uuid "e91c4afa-4ad3-5bf8-8c22-27e71bd7cdd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf K(x,y,z)=\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685031} :answer-field/id #uuid "7117e5bd-6fe0-50ab-a688-66f0465c897a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dc8be64f-41e6-5ea1-8766-587f3252c67f" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7a0a919af689e9c332ba6ceb3d606208dab9eabadef9b4871ac8e164843ebe88.png)\n\nCompare the arrows with the positive directions of the labeled axes. The listed formulas are constant vector fields. Which could generate the field shown?\n\nArrow lengths are drawn using a common display scale; no numerical magnitude is specified." :question/worked-solution "Each arrow is parallel to the $z$-axis and points in its positive direction. Thus the $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ components are zero, while the $\\mathbf k$ component is positive.\n\nThe field $\\mathbf F=-\\mathbf k$ points in the opposite direction. The fields $\\mathbf G=\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf K=\\mathbf j$ point along the wrong axes.\n\nAll the displayed arrows have the same length, consistent with a constant field. Therefore $\\mathbf H(x,y,z)=\\mathbf k$ could generate the diagram. Since a listed formula fits, “None of the listed” is incorrect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186685343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03fda3fe-b570-50cd-90f2-bfdc3cc9df2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685338} {:answer/id #uuid "2a1515d3-a5a9-525a-9e8f-c3f427a3424c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf K(x,y,z)=y^{2}\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685340} {:answer/id #uuid "69e7ea72-6a3e-5be9-bb8a-968808d9a5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf H(x,y,z)=- y\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685344} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba1ad09-bd08-5db3-8f51-94ddabe88296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf G(x,y,z)=e^{y}\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685345} {:answer/id #uuid "a265e073-d932-5b61-a6e5-e84d306d5c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186685348}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 175921